From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:22:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] freebsd: run Linux images through a runtime handler
 (Linuxulator)

FreeBSD runs Linux ELF binaries directly under the Linux ABI (linux64.ko),
in jails like any container; podman already uses this. Let CRI-O do it for
Kubernetes pods whose RuntimeClass maps to a runtime handler with
default_annotations io.bsdk8s.image-os = "linux":

- pull: images for such pods are pulled for that OS instead of the host's
  (the CRI passes the runtime handler with pulls only behind the alpha
  RuntimeClassInImageCriApi gate, but the kubelet creates the sandbox
  first, so it is found by the pod UID);
- create: containers of Linux images get /proc (linprocfs), /sys
  (linsysfs) and /dev/shm (tmpfs), as podman gives Linux containers;
  mounts the pod supplies win.

No change for other platforms. Test.
